------------------------------------------------------------
COMMUNICATION LATENCY MODEL ASSUMPTIONS
------------------------------------------------------------
- LOCAL decisions have L_i = 0.
- For every remote choice p > 0, upload scales with p.
- For every remote choice p > 0, download uses the integral remote output.
- L(C) is the sum of the task communication latencies, not their average.
- tau_n is included once as aggregated end-to-end propagation delay.
- tau_n is independent of p and excludes bandwidth-dependent transfer times.

